## Procedure

1. Launch Gophish and open its local administrative interface.
2. Create the SMTP profile and send a test message only to the designated lab mailbox.
3. Create the email template using the source fragment and verify placeholder substitution.
4. Create a landing page explaining the simulation and its warning signs. Leave capture of submitted data and passwords disabled for this awareness exercise.
5. Add the consenting test group. Configure a campaign URL reachable by those lab clients. `127.0.0.1` only reaches the same machine and is unsuitable as a shared remote-client destination.
6. Launch the authorised campaign and observe the timeline.
7. Record sent, opened and clicked counts with the limits of the tracking mechanism.
8. Discuss the suspicious message cues and the appropriate reporting procedure.

## Observations and result

The handout's numerical example gives 20 sent messages and six clicks, yielding 6/20 × 100 = 30% when sent messages are used as the denominator. State the denominator and whether counts represent unique recipients. Use actual lab measurements for the final record. In the awareness-only configuration, submitted-data collection remains disabled.

Training, a clear reporting channel, careful sender/link checking and MFA reduce risk. SPF, DKIM and DMARC support domain authentication and policy handling, while filtering and attachment controls address additional paths. These controls complement user education.

